[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Findings that shape this table:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **No function returns a value.** All five exported functions are `void`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   There is no error code, no sentinel return, no `errno` use, no `assert`, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   no `exit`/`abort`. Therefore "same error/rejection" is observable **only**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   through the bytes written to `stdout` (and through not crashing).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * There are exactly **two** conditional branches in the entire library:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * `driver.c:32` — `if (line != NULL)` in `printLine` (a null check),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * `driver.c:61` — `if (fabs(data) > 0.000001)` in `goodB2G` (a range check),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     with its `else` at `driver.c:66`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `bad()` (`driver.c:43-47`) has **no** guard at all. Its "error" behaviour is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the C undefined behaviour of `(int)double` when the value does not fit an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `int`. The shipped binary implements this with `cvttsd2si`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`objdump -d`, `bad+0x22`), which yields the *integer indefinite* value
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `INT_MIN` = `-2147483648` for NaN and for every out-of-range magnitude.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   That is the ground truth the Rust must reproduce (it does, via `to_c_int`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * There are **no enums anywhere** in the public API, so "out-of-range enum
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   value across FFI" degenerates to "out-of-range *float* bit pattern", which
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   rows 12-18 cover (signalling/quiet NaN, ±inf, subnormals, ±max).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
